        "updated_at": "2025-01-01T15:19:37Z",
        "author_association": "OWNER",
        "body": "Not exactly what I wanted, but it doesn't matter tbh as it will likely depend in screen size anyway. The goal is to have the iframe to be as big as it can get without leaving the bottom of the screen under the answer buttons. So at 50% it fits within the screen but doesn't take up the entire height, which means wasted space. This is mainly a concern with the backside as you want to be able to see as much as possible with the board moves. \r\n\r\nI made an estimate based in the videos you sent and a ruler, and It looks to be the sweet spot at about 77vh. Last release should display better. Let me know how you go with it.  I should be able to avoid similar issues in future. It's easier If I know an appropriate height for the iframe. ",
